<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If8c956755e12bc5e0c5153f46f86fa874b018654" commit="8aa11a7e042443356543e38a3425ab55d4dab829" commit_message="CRAS: dev_stream - Remove unused argument dev_index of dev_stream_capture  Also remove the unused arguments related to dev_index in audio_thread.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50139 TEST=make check  Signed-off-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: If8c956755e12bc5e0c5153f46f86fa874b018654 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/332911 Reviewed-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="332911" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/11/332911/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I814efec846140dfec75e51967017fe5473e8b9c3" commit="07e83f6fb2fa497dad7d037bddfccc7e35872907" commit_message="CRAS: alsa_ucm : Add flag to enable software gain  There are boards without any gain control for internal microphone. To apply software gain on this node, user can specify MaxSoftwareGain &quot;2000&quot; in SectionDevice for internal microphon. The system capture gain limit will be -5000 to 2000 dBm. Note that if there is capture gain control in mixer or on the node, then the combined hardware gain will be set to 0dB if software gain is used. The following patch series will implement the above feature.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50139 TEST=make check  Signed-off-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I814efec846140dfec75e51967017fe5473e8b9c3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/332914 Reviewed-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="332914" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/14/332914/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib6a2ffb5c607220f7539bbbe8c40561d7952689d" commit="1f69fabd6e5434630ee399363463855efcea386c" commit_message="CRAS: iodev - Add fields related to software gain in cras_ionode  Reuse flag software_volume_needed to enable/disable software gain on an input node. Use max_software_gain to store maximum software gain. Only enable this flag for input on ALSA ionode where UCM MaxSoftwareGain is set. If there are capture gain controls on this alsa_input_node, their combined gain will be set to 0dB in set_alsa_capture_gain when software gain is used.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50139 TEST=make check  Signed-off-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: Ib6a2ffb5c607220f7539bbbe8c40561d7952689d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/332915 Reviewed-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="332915" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/15/332915/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id4fb5acee92af80690f927ae741a8db0e74f4abd" commit="9de347fed677f60b5e6ae5f1fdec3e22f9324a32" commit_message="CRAS: iodev - Add a method to query software gain scaler  The gain should be applied is the sum of system gain and node gain. Convert the gain from dB * 100 to a scaler.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50139 TEST=make check  Signed-off-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: Id4fb5acee92af80690f927ae741a8db0e74f4abd Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/332916 Reviewed-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="332916" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/16/332916/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8b6286f40bb1a21afde30f8825c9e562c7398e50" commit="966fbe7f3944c018e81c2335f7b006fb625a1738" commit_message="CRAS: alsa_io - Set capture gain limits for software gain  Use max_software_gain when software gain is needed. Otherwise, Cras client will see the gain range is 0dB to 0dB and can not use software gain properly. Use the default minimum value for minimum because that value does not matter.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50139 TEST=make check TEST=cras_test_client --dump_s and check the system capture gain range is not 0-0 on software gain case.  Signed-off-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I8b6286f40bb1a21afde30f8825c9e562c7398e50 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/333242 Reviewed-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="333242" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/42/333242/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5357ceb3ed04fdf19f7fe54bcdd4eeeb571cab70" commit="45830f87694b3ac7ebe24da3e50c6a9cf47ee80e" commit_message="Sentry: UCM config: Set Mic Volume to 24dB  The default value of &quot;Mic Volume&quot; control is 0dB which is too low. This patch sets the gain to +24dB.  This patch also binds the &quot;Mic Volume&quot; control to the sklnau8825max Headset Jack, so that CRAS can adjust it at runtime for AGC.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:51527 TEST=The remote side can hear clearly in hangouts. See &quot;cras_test_client --capture_gain ...&quot; affects &